In article <1992Sep5.012331.20022@polari>, gregs@polari.online.com writes...
>angus@hardy.u.washington.edu (Angus the Demonchild) writes:
>>Crystal balls will allow you to know the positions of every item of
>>one particular type on your dungeon level, like a selective potion of
>>object detection.  
> 
>Ok, but how do you do it?  It asks, "What do you want to detect?" or
>something like that.  What are the proper answers?  I'm pretty sure that
>"!" will detect potions, and "?" scrolls, but what about "objects" (Like
>the generic potion.)  What about Monsters?  

Crystal balls will detect five different things: gold, food, traps, objects
(other than food), and monsters.  It's fairly adaptable about how you answer
the question, but for example you can answer $, %, ^, objects, and monsters.
They are not selective on type of object.  Whether you ask for ! or ? or =,
you still get shown all kinds of objects.  Note that the crystal ball doesn't
always work, and it comes with a fixed number of charges (like a wand)
after which it certainly won't work.  There's a chance it'll do you a
variety of types of harm, particularly if cursed.  They also weigh a ton.

